# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Throwaway runs produced by tools/sandbox-check.sh.
# That tool installs into a fake HOME to prove the manager never touches your
# real configuration; this is where it writes the run it leaves behind for
# inspection (report.txt, stdout.clean, stderr.clean).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.sandbox-e2e/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# App-generated MACHINE STATE — must never be committed.
# These files record this machine's sessions and absolute paths; syncing them
# to another computer breaks (or leaks) rather than helps.
#
# NOTE: identity files are intentionally NOT ignored. This repository IS the
# sync mechanism for user config (see README "Privacy"), so
# config/git/config.ini and config/git/work.ini stay tracked by design.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/state.json
**/session*
**/*.sock
**/*.pid
**/*.lock
**/*.log
.DS_Store
